<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #3950.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="259974214" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/kafka/issues/3950" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/kafka/pull/3950/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/3950">#3950</a> from manjuapu/customer-logo-stream

This PR is the first of several subtasks for [KAFKA-2376](<a href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-2376" rel="nofollow">https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-2376</a>) to add metrics to Connect worker processes. See that issue and [KIP-196 for details](<a href="https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-196%3A+Add+metrics+to+Kafka+Connect+framework" rel="nofollow">https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-196%3A+Add+metrics+to+Kafka+Connect+framework</a>).

This PR adds metrics for each connector using Kafka’s existing `Metrics` framework. This is the first of several changes to add several groups of metrics, this change starts by adding a very simple `ConnectMetrics` object that is owned by each worker and that makes it easy to define multiple groups of metrics, called `ConnectMetricGroup` objects. Each metric group maps to a JMX MBean, and each metric within the group maps to an MBean attribute.

Future PRs will build upon this simple pattern to add metrics for source and sink tasks, workers, and worker rebalances.

